12835	{"artifactId":"HLD-b7a68147dcf72034","entry":{"id":"review-52d0c0827b347c235e4411207f44e44e","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:26:44.174Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every DEF acceptance criterion for s1–s7 has a home in the HLD's story boundaries and pipeline order (hooks run only on success and in order; checked typed result; per-call approval with no bypass; git/gh/Jira families keep their ids; cutover with a build check and a call-site list).","evidence":"DEF.md §6.1–6.7: s1 ac1–ac5, s2 ac1–ac6, s3 ac1–ac7, s4–s6 ac1–ac6 and s7 ac1–ac6 each match an element of HLD §3 (steps 1–6) and §5.1–5.7. Example: s3 ac3 ('denied … for lack of an answer') matches ApprovalDenial 'timed-out' | 'no-client'. s7 ac6 matches the inventory kept in docs/plans/tool-registry.md. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No DEF non-goal is built: the hooks stay inside the executor, there are no shims or phased migration, and git run outside the daemon is not captured.","evidence":"DEF.md:72-77 non-goals: 'A hook mechanism outside the tool executor', 'A phased migration or compatibility shims', 'Capturing git run in a terminal or IDE outside the daemon'. The HLD puts hooks at step 5 of executeTool, makes the cutover one change with no shims (k6), and leaves the plugin's git runner out of scope. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool today runs approval-flagged tools as approved: an 'auto-approving' fallback exists in executor.ts and there is no gate, schema check or hook stage.","evidence":"src/daemon/tools/executor.ts:41-48: 'const needsGate = tool.requiresApproval === true || …; if (needsGate) { log.warn(…, \"…auto-approving\"); } … return await tool.execute(input, deps);'. There is no output check and no hooks. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Of the git tools, only git_push and git_reset ask for approval on every call today, so narrowing 'destructive' to pushes and merges keeps unattended workflows running (HLD §5.4, §6 Security, Risky bits).","evidence":"Many more git builtins declare 'requiresApproval: true': git/commit.ts:49, git/stage.ts:43, git/pull.ts:37, git/merge.ts:38, git/checkout.ts:45, git/rebase.ts:46, git/amend.ts:46, git/revert.ts:36, git/cherry-pick.ts:33. Branch, tag, stash, remote and worktree use input-dependent predicates. Once s3 maps the existing flags to the destructive marker, commit, stage and pull will also ask, and fail with no client attached until s4 narrows them. The risk mitigation names only 'pushes and merges'. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/commit.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/stage.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/pull.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/reset.ts]","action":"Correct the description of current behaviour: list every git and gh tool that is approval-flagged today. Make the Phase A→B window explicit: either s3 does not map the flags until s4 and s5 land, or the LLDs list commit, stage and pull among the calls that will ask.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared failure kinds reuse the kinds the tracker port already uses (missing-tool, missing-signin, unreachable, rejected).","evidence":"src/workflow/tracker/port.ts:23: 'export type PortFailureKind = 'missing-tool' | 'missing-signin' | 'unreachable' | 'rejected';'. sc5's ToolFailureKind is a superset of these kinds that adds timed-out, conversion-failed, schema-mismatch and denied. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The destructive marker is new, while the existing requiresApproval field (boolean or input predicate) is the thing that gets mapped onto it.","evidence":"src/daemon/tools/types.ts:118: 'readonly requiresApproval?: boolean | ((input: ToolInput) => boolean);'. No 'destructive' field exists today. sc2's 'destructive?: boolean | ((input: I) => boolean)' copies that shape. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Settle in the s2 and s3 LLDs whether 'destructive' replaces requiresApproval or sits beside it (already listed as an open question).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There are 22 runGit calls in production code.","evidence":"rg 'runGit\\(' in src: policy-reader 8, anchor-finder 2, sighting-store 1, signoff 3, handoff 7, policy-refresh 1, git.ts 1 (the definition), plus 2 in a test. That gives 22 production calls. [files: src/workflow/team/git.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"commitAndPushArtifacts has 5 callers across 4 files.","evidence":"signoff.ts:385, cli/services/workflow.ts:139 and :174, resolve-comment.ts:218, questions.ts:470. That is 5 calls in 4 files, plus tracker.test.ts. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The github.ts wrappers have 3 importers, and the cutover touches about 10 source files.","evidence":"github.ts exports about 30 shell-out wrappers (runGh, ghCreateIssue, ghComment, ghCloseIssue, queryTasks, …). The production files that import it include signoff.ts, tracker/github-adapter.ts, cli/services/workflow.ts, tracker/sync.ts, tracker/attach.ts, tracker-auto.ts, questions.ts, bugfix/tracker.ts, resolve-comment.ts and tracker/setup.ts, plus about 12 tests that use it. That is far more than 3 importers, and with the 6 team files more than 10 source files. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts, src/workflow/tracker/attach.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/bugfix/tracker.ts, src/workflow/tracker/setup.ts]","action":"Rebuild the call-site inventory in docs/plans/tool-registry.md from a full source search of github.ts importers and size s7 from it. The 'one change' cutover is larger than stated.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"sc2's ToolDefinition can be added without breaking the existing builtins, and tools with no schema are left unchecked (Rollout Phase A).","evidence":"The sc2 sketch declares 'outputSchema: JsonSchema' as required, but about 110 existing builtins have no output schema and ToolResult (types.ts:33) carries only 'output: string'. The rollout says 'A tool with no declared output schema is not checked', which needs the field to be optional. The two statements contradict each other. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Make outputSchema optional in sc2 (outputSchema?: JsonSchema), or state that s2 adds a schema to every builtin.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored shape changes: pending approvals live in memory and count as denied after a restart, hooks are registered in code, and artifacts, commits and tracker records stay unchanged and are checked by the existing stage tests.","evidence":"HLD §6 Durability and Phase C backward compat. DEF s7 ac3 asks for the same artifacts, commits and tracker records, and tracker.test.ts already exercises commitAndPushArtifacts. The executor persists nothing today (executor.ts is stateless). [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/tracker.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"s7's boundary covers only what the Epic's s7 criteria ask for.","evidence":"HLD §5.7 adds 'the registration of the first real hook for the team-signoff Story s9'. DEF.md §6.7 s7 ac1–ac6 cover moving call sites, deleting old paths, the build check, the same artifacts, the hook firing for workflow calls and the denial. None of them registers the team-signoff s9 hook, which belongs to the other Epic. The HLD itself lists this as an open question. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Remove the s9 hook registration from s7's boundary, or amend the DEF to add it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Each shared contract has exactly one owner Story and no Story redesigns another Story's contract.","evidence":"The destructive marker sits in sc2's ToolDefinition sketch (owned by s2), yet §5.3 says s3 owns 'the destructive marker on a tool definition'. That gives the field two owners. Today the matching field is requiresApproval in src/daemon/tools/types.ts:118. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Assign the destructive field to one contract, preferably sc4 owned by s3, and remove it from sc2.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A missing acli is told apart from a signed-out acli with 'acli jira auth status' plus a PATH lookup, because failing commands do not say which.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md:44: 'signed out: acli jira auth status prints \"unauthorized: …\", exit 1; other commands only say e.g. \"failed to list projects\" … sign-in must be checked with auth status first'. Lines 40-41 record the --yes and bounded-search requirements that s6 adopts. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every pipeline failure can be detected by the caller: a denial (declined, timed-out, no-client), a schema mismatch, a conversion failure and a hook failure are each returned on the result and not thrown.","evidence":"sc4 ApprovalDenial, sc5 ToolFailureKind (denied, schema-mismatch, conversion-failed, timed-out) and sc1 HookFailure[] on the result. HLD §3 says 'A failed or denied call never reaches step 5'. This matches DEF s1 ac2/ac3 and s3 ac3/ac4. Today executor.ts:47-57 already turns thrown errors into success:false results. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The highest-risk criteria have tests planned at HLD level: stage order (denied call never runs the tool, failed or mismatching call never runs a hook, hook failure keeps success), replay of captured CLI output through the cheap and escalated conversion paths, and the existing stage tests as the cutover check.","evidence":"HLD Risky bits table, mitigation column, covers DEF s1 ac2/ac3, s2 ac4/ac6, s3 ac4 and s7 ac3. Mapping each remaining criterion to a test is left to the Story LLDs, which suits an HLD. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Each LLD must map its Story's criteria to named tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":5,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T09:26:44.174Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
