11577	{"artifactId":"HLD-b7a68147dcf72034","entry":{"id":"review-89da3c1bd19d7ca18173a9515c042577","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:33:39.534Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The seven HLD Stories (hooks, typed result, approval, git, gh, Jira, cutover) cover the DEF's Stories one-to-one.","evidence":"DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json has s1 'Run a rule once after a tool succeeds', s2 'Give every tool a checked, typed result', s3 'Ask the user before any destructive operation, every time', s4 git, s5 gh, s6 Jira via acli, s7 cutover; each maps to a §5 boundary. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Narrowing the git/gh approval flags so commit, stage and pull never ask is consistent with the DEF's s3 acceptance criteria.","evidence":"DEF s3 ac6: 'given a tool that today declares it needs approval and is run as if approved, when the change is complete, then it asks for approval before it runs'. git commit.ts:49, stage.ts:43 and pull.ts:37 set requiresApproval: true today, and the HLD (§3, §5.4, phase B) says s4/s5 replace those flags so commit, stage and pull do not ask. docs/plans/tool-registry.md line 51 records the facts but no decision that amends ac6. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/commit.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Either amend DEF s3 ac6 (and record the decision in docs/plans/tool-registry.md) to say that git/gh flags are narrowed to the operations that can destroy work, or keep ac6 and drop the narrowing.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today executeTool treats requiresApproval (boolean or predicate) as approved and runs the tool, logging 'auto-approving'.","evidence":"executor.ts:41-45: needsGate computed from tool.requiresApproval === true or the predicate; then log.warn(..., 'tool requires approval but the gate dispatcher is gone; auto-approving') and the tool runs at line 48. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"requiresApproval is true on 11 git tools, a predicate on 5 more, and true on 27 gh operations.","evidence":"grep: true on amend, checkout, cherry-pick, commit, merge, pull, push, rebase, reset, revert, stage (11); a predicate function on branch, remote, stash, tag, worktree (5); gh true: repo 4, release 4, issue 5, actions 3, project 4, pr 7 = 27. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The tracker port already defines the failure kinds missing-tool / missing-signin / unreachable / rejected that sc5 extends.","evidence":"src/workflow/tracker/port.ts:23 `export type PortFailureKind = 'missing-tool' | 'missing-signin' | 'unreachable' | 'rejected';` [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No approval exchange from the daemon to the client exists today, so sc4's approval.request/approval.answer IPC is new work that s3 must build.","evidence":"src/daemon/server.ts dispatches request.method to handlers/streamHandlers and only writes responses (socket.write at line 103); it has no notify, broadcast or server-initiated request path. The executor header confirms the old gate dispatcher was removed. The DEF s3 FR says the exchange is built in this Story. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The typed helper 'takes a tool id and input and returns a result typed from the schema'.","evidence":"§3 and §8.1 say the helper takes a tool id (a string), but the sc2 sketch is `callTool<T extends OutputSchemaField<any>>(tool: T, input: ToolInput<T>, deps)`, which infers the type from a tool object. A string id cannot carry outputType unless there is a typed id-to-tool map, and the HLD defines none. Building from the prose as written loses the typing, which the HLD itself lists as a con of a1. [files: src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Pick one form in sc2: either the helper takes the tool definition object (callers import it), or add a typed id-to-definition map that the helper keys on. Make §3 and §8.1 match.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There are 22 runGit calls in 6 production files under src/workflow/team, plus git.ts, which defines runGit.","evidence":"grep runGit(: policy-reader 8, handoff 7, signoff 3, anchor-finder 2, sighting-store 1, policy-refresh 1 = 22, plus git.ts 1 (the definition). [files: src/workflow/team]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/workflow/tracker/github.ts has 11 production importers, and commitAndPushArtifacts has 5 call sites.","evidence":"Importers: cli/services/workflow.ts, team/signoff.ts, tracker/attach.ts, tracker/sync.ts, tracker-auto.ts, tracker/setup.ts, tracker/github-adapter.ts, questions.ts, bugfix/tracker.ts, resolve-comment.ts, config/github.ts (11). Call sites: signoff.ts:385, resolve-comment.ts:218, cli/services/workflow.ts:139 and :174, questions.ts:470 (5). [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The about-17-file call-site inventory covers every place the backend spawns git or gh outside src/daemon/tools, so the build check can land without breaking the build.","evidence":"grep for execFileSync/execFile/exec('git'|'gh') outside src/daemon/tools finds direct spawns the inventory does not list: src/workflow/team/git-async.ts:40 (execFile('git'), used by handoff.ts, policy-refresh.ts and branch-resolution.ts), src/daemon/steps/build-step/validation-checks.ts:155,220,380, src/daemon/installed-commit.ts:46, src/workflow/gates.ts:597, src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:67, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/header.ts:148, src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts:97,264,273, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts:243, src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts:97,235, and attach.ts:55, which has its own git helper beside its github.js import. That is at least 10 more production files. docs/plans/tool-registry.md mentions none of them. The repository check described in §3 and §5.7 would fail on all of them, and the 'about 17 files' sizing of s7 is too small. [files: src/workflow/team/git-async.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/validation-checks.ts, src/daemon/installed-commit.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/convert/plan.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/header.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/workflow/tracker/attach.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Rebuild the inventory now in docs/plans/tool-registry.md from the spawn search, not only from the runGit and github.js imports, and list each file. Size s7 from that list, or state which spawns, if any (for example installed-commit.ts for the daemon's own checkout), are exempt from the build check and why.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored shape changes: pending approvals live in memory, hooks are registered in code, and the artifacts, commits and tracker records stay the same; adding the optional outputSchema leaves the roughly 110 builtins without one unchanged.","evidence":"executor.ts returns a ToolResult with output: string and no persisted state. docs/plans/tool-registry.md:53 records that about 110 builtins have no output schema, so it must be optional; the HLD makes outputSchema optional (sc2) and describes no migration of stored records. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each shared contract has exactly one owner Story, and the family Stories (s4 to s6) only consume sc2 to sc5 and do not redesign them.","evidence":"§4: sc1 is owned by s1; sc2, sc3 and sc5 by s2; sc4 by s3. §5.4 to §5.7 list only 'Depends on'. s3 explicitly leaves the choice of destructive operations to each family Story, matching DEF s4/s5/s6. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every failure has a detectable kind and a stated handling: denial (declined, timed-out, no-client), schema mismatch, conversion failure, hook failure reported on the result, and a pending request at restart treated as denied.","evidence":"sc4 ApprovalDenial and sc5 ToolFailureKind cover 'denied', 'schema-mismatch' and 'conversion-failed'; sc1 HookFailure goes on the result; §6 Durability says a request left open at restart is denied. Today the executor returns success:false with an error on a throw (executor.ts:49-57), which the new kinds refine. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The highest-risk acceptance criteria (stage order: a denied call never runs the tool, a failed or mismatching call never runs a hook, a hook failure does not change success; conversion accuracy) are mapped to tests.","evidence":"§7 Risky bits: 'Pin the stage order with tests that assert it directly ...' and 'tests replay captured real CLI output through both the cheap and the escalated path, including truncated and made-up values'; s7's check is the existing stage tests. The test mapping for each acceptance criterion is left to the LLDs, which fits an HLD.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":2,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T09:33:39.534Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
