10634	{"artifactId":"HLD-b7a68147dcf72034","entry":{"id":"review-ef65bda005ac6659f2804e6555ea4681","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:43:17.307Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The HLD designs every DEF requirement on result shapes: the output schema is optional and about 110 builtins 'stay unchecked until their family Story adds one'.","evidence":"DEF S002:FR001 says 'A tool without a declared result shape cannot be registered.' FR004 says 'Every tool declares the shape of its result, the executor checks each result against it'. The HLD's sc2 has `outputSchema?: JsonSchema` and §3 says the builtins without one 'stay unchecked'. tool-registry.md:53 records why ('ToolResult.output is a string, so outputSchema has to be optional'). The HLD's Open questions list only the ac6 reading, so this departure from S002:FR001/FR004 is neither designed nor flagged for a DEF amendment. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Add an open question or DEF amendment for S002:FR001/FR004 (optional schema, unchecked builtins), or design how registration rejects a tool with no schema.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The sc4 ApprovalRequest carries what the DEF requires the approval request to name.","evidence":"DEF S003:FR001: 'The approval request names the tool, the repository and the arguments it would run with.' The sc4 sketch has `{ requestId; toolId; approvalClass; inputSummary; reason; expiresAt }`. There is no repository field, and the arguments appear only as a free-form 'inputSummary'. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Add the repository (repoPath from ToolDeps) and the exact arguments to ApprovalRequest in sc4.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the executor treats a tool's requiresApproval flag as approved and runs it, so no tool asks.","evidence":"executor.ts:41-48 computes needsGate for `=== true` or a predicate, logs 'tool requires approval but the gate dispatcher is gone; auto-approving' and then calls tool.execute.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The flag is true on 11 git tools, a predicate on 5 (branch, remote, stash, tag, worktree), true on 27 gh operations, and set in other families; there are 22 git ids.","evidence":"In builtins/git it is true on amend, checkout, cherry-pick, commit, merge, pull, push, rebase, reset, revert and stage; a predicate on branch, remote, stash, tag and worktree; false on blame, diff, fetch, log, show and status (22 files). The gh true counts are repo 4, release 4, issue 5, actions 3, project 4 and pr 7, which is 27. The flag also appears in the file, cloud, k8s, ssh, http and other builtins.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"sc4's approval field is 'the one field that gives a tool or call its approval class', and the destructive class is new, marked by the family Stories.","evidence":"types.ts:127-128 already declares `readonly destructive?: boolean` on Tool ('Flags the tool as destructive / irreversible'). 8 builtins set `destructive: true`: az/vm.ts:238, k8s/index.ts:340, aws/s3.ts:210, gcp/compute.ts:247, aws/cloudformation.ts:235, gcp/run.ts:212, gcp/storage.ts:189 and aws/ec2.ts:255. types.ts:83-145 also has ToolApprovalGate / buildApprovalGate. The HLD mentions neither. s3 maps only requiresApproval to 'common', so these 8 tools would be downgraded to 'common', or a second field would be left beside the new one. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/cloud/aws/s3.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/k8s/index.ts]","action":"In s3, map `destructive: true` to the destructive class (or retire the field) and say how buildApprovalGate relates to ApprovalRequest.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The tool hook registry and the output-schema field are new and do not already exist in the tool layer.","evidence":"A grep for registerToolHook, toolHook, afterTool and outputSchema in src finds only analyze planner templates (an unrelated outputSchema). Nothing under src/daemon/tools.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Hooks receive `caller: 'agent' | 'daemon' | 'workflow'` in ToolHookContext, which the executor can supply.","evidence":"`executeTool(toolId, input, deps)` (executor.ts:23) takes no caller identity, and ToolDeps (types.ts:50-81) has no caller field. The only production caller is read-only-tool-loop.ts:78. Neither sc1 nor sc2 (callTool takes `deps: ToolDeps`) says where the caller value comes from, or which signature or ToolDeps change carries it. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"State in sc1/sc2 the field that carries the caller (for example `ToolDeps.caller`) and who sets it on each path.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The direct-spawn inventory (17 files that spawn the CLI, including maintenance.ts, identity.ts, indexer/index.ts and repo-ignore-filter.ts, plus 15 wrapper callers) matches the code.","evidence":"A grep for execFile/spawn/exec with 'git'/'gh' finds 13 of the listed files. maintenance.ts uses capture('git', ...) and stream('git', ...) (17 sites), identity.ts runs ['gh', ...] and ['git', ...], and indexer/index.ts:91 and repo-ignore-filter.ts:112 pass 'git'. runGit and commitAndPushArtifacts callers are in workflow/team/*, questions.ts, resolve-comment.ts and cli/services/workflow.ts, as listed.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"sc5 failure kinds are 'the same kinds the tracker port already uses'.","evidence":"port.ts:23 has `PortFailureKind = 'missing-tool' | 'missing-signin' | 'unreachable' | 'rejected'`, and github.ts:76 maps a timeout to 'unreachable'. sc5 adds 'timed-out', 'conversion-failed', 'schema-mismatch' and 'denied'. unit-issue.test.ts:390 iterates exactly the four port kinds. The HLD gives no mapping from the new kinds onto PortFailureKind for the tracker port and its stored or tested results, even though s7 promises 'the same tracker records as before'. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/unit-issue.test.ts]","action":"State in sc5 or s7 how the new kinds map onto PortFailureKind, or that PortFailureKind is widened and its consumers updated.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Story ownership is consistent with the DEF: s3 owns the approval field and exchange while s4-s6 only mark their own destructive operations, and s7 depends on s1-s5 (not s6).","evidence":"In the DEF, s4, s5 and s6 each depend on s2 and s3, and s7 on s1-s5. In the HLD, s4-s6 consume sc2, sc3, sc4 and sc5, and s7 consumes sc1, sc2, sc4 and sc5. §5.3 says s3 'does not choose which individual git, gh or Jira operations are destructive'. DEF s4/s5/s6 ac3/ac4 put destructive marking in the family Stories.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every caller's call reaches an approval gate that sends the request 'over the daemon's IPC to the attached client'.","evidence":"maintenance.ts:81-83 ('Fast-forward sync + conditional install + build against DAEMON_ROOT. Never starts the daemon.') runs in the terminal client process. It runs git checkout -B, merge and remote set-url, often while the daemon is not running. cli/services/workflow.ts calls commitAndPushArtifacts (:139, :174). Both move onto the registry under s7, but the HLD only describes a daemon-side gate. It does not say which process runs the executor for these callers, or what the ApprovalGate does there (with no daemon a destructive call would always be 'no-client'). [files: src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"State in s3/s7 whether CLI-process callers go through daemon IPC or an in-process gate, and how the self-update works when the daemon is down.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to a test, including S007:FR001 ('each replaced call site is covered by a test that runs through the registry').","evidence":"The HLD names tests for the pipeline order (risk table) and replayed CLI output for conversion. For the cutover it says only 'the existing tests of those stages are the check' (§7 Phase C). DEF S007:FR001 requires a registry-path test per replaced site. Sites such as indexer/index.ts:91, repo-ignore-filter.ts:112 and identity.ts are not covered by any workflow-stage test. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Add to s7's boundary that each inventoried site gets a test through the registry (or through the typed helper with a recorded executor).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":7,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T09:43:17.307Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
